{
  "title": "Phase 1 · Stage 2: The command loop",
  "summary": "Turn the card into an interactive program: read commands until the input ends, and validate what you are given.",
  "minutes": 25,
  "prereqs": [
    "csharp/02-control-flow/01-booleans-and-if",
    "csharp/02-control-flow/02-switch",
    "csharp/02-control-flow/03-while-loops",
    "csharp/01-first-steps/05-input-and-conversion"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "A program that listens",
      "body": [
        "A librarian does not restart Shelfwise for every book. From now on the program is a **command loop**: it reads one line at a time, works out which command it is, does it, and goes back for the next line, until the input ends or the user types `quit`.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
        "stats",
        "quit",
        "```",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line == \"\") continue;          // skip blank lines",
        "",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string command = space < 0 ? line : line.Substring(0, space);",
        "    string rest = space < 0 ? \"\" : line.Substring(space + 1).Trim();",
        "",
        "    if (command == \"quit\") break;      // leave the loop",
        "",
        "    switch (command)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"help\": Console.WriteLine(\"...\"); break;",
        "        default: Console.WriteLine($\"Unknown command: {command}\"); break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Bye.\");",
        "```",
        "",
        "The `while` condition reads *and* tests in one go: assign the line, then check it is not `null` (end of input). `continue` jumps to the next line; `break` leaves the loop. Because `Bye.` is printed **after** the loop, it appears whether the user typed `quit` or the input simply ended."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "The input is five lines: `a`, an empty line, `b`, `quit`, then `c`. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "string? line;",
        "int count = 0;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    if (line == \"\") continue;",
        "    if (line == \"quit\") break;",
        "    count++;",
        "}",
        "Console.WriteLine(count);"
      ],
      "answer": "2",
      "stdin": "a\n\nb\nquit\nc",
      "explain": "The blank line is skipped by `continue`, `a` and `b` are counted, `quit` breaks out before `c` is read."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "The user types `add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3`. After `rest.Split('|')`, what is `parts[3]`?",
      "options": [
        "`\"1937\"`",
        "`1937`",
        "`\"J.R.R. Tolkien\"`",
        "`\"3\"`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Indexes start at 0: isbn, title, author, **year**, copies. And it is still the *text* `\"1937\"` until you parse it."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "carry": true,
      "title": "Read commands",
      "prompt": [
        "Replace the card with a command loop. Keep `library` and `version`; drop the rest of stage 1 (its variables are no longer needed).",
        "",
        "1. First print `Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.`",
        "2. Read lines until the input ends. Trim each line and skip blank ones.",
        "3. Split each line into a **command** (up to the first space) and the **rest**.",
        "4. Commands:",
        "   - `help` prints `Commands: add, stats, help, quit`",
        "   - `add isbn|title|author|year|copies` counts one more book and adds its copies, then prints `Added: <title> (<year>)`",
        "   - `stats` prints `Books: <n> | Copies: <n>`",
        "   - `quit` stops reading",
        "   - anything else prints `Unknown command: <command>`",
        "5. After the loop, always print `Bye.`",
        "",
        "Input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
        "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|2",
        "stats",
        "quit",
        "```",
        "",
        "Output:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
        "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
        "Added: Dune (1965)",
        "Books: 2 | Copies: 5",
        "Bye.",
        "```",
        "",
        "Every `add` line in this step is well formed, so `int.Parse` is fine."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "const int CurrentYear = 2026;",
        "",
        "string library = \"Shelfwise\";",
        "int version = 1;",
        "",
        "decimal finePerDay = 0.50m;",
        "",
        "string isbn = Console.ReadLine() ?? \"\";",
        "string title = Console.ReadLine() ?? \"\";",
        "string author = Console.ReadLine() ?? \"\";",
        "int year = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine() ?? \"0\");",
        "int copies = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine() ?? \"0\");",
        "int age = CurrentYear - year;",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{library} v{version}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{title} by {author} ({year})\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"ISBN: {isbn}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Copies: {copies}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Age: {age} years\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Fine per day: {finePerDay:C}\");",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"|{title,-24}|{author,-18}|{year,5}|{copies,3}|\");"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "string library = \"Shelfwise\";",
        "int version = 1;",
        "int books = 0;",
        "int copies = 0;",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{library} v{version}. Type help for commands.\");",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line == \"\") continue;",
        "",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string command = space < 0 ? line : line.Substring(0, space);",
        "    string rest = space < 0 ? \"\" : line.Substring(space + 1).Trim();",
        "",
        "    if (command == \"quit\") break;",
        "",
        "    switch (command)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"help\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine(\"Commands: add, stats, help, quit\");",
        "            break;",
        "        case \"add\":",
        "        {",
        "            string[] parts = rest.Split('|');",
        "            int year = int.Parse(parts[3]);",
        "            int count = int.Parse(parts[4]);",
        "            books++;",
        "            copies += count;",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Added: {parts[1]} ({year})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"stats\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Books: {books} | Copies: {copies}\");",
        "            break;",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Unknown command: {command}\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Bye.\");"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "add two books and ask for stats",
          "stdin": [
            "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
            "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|2",
            "stats",
            "quit"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
            "Added: Dune (1965)",
            "Books: 2 | Copies: 5",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "help, blank lines and an unknown command",
          "stdin": [
            "help",
            "",
            "   stats",
            "dance"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Commands: add, stats, help, quit",
            "Books: 0 | Copies: 0",
            "Unknown command: dance",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "quit stops reading",
          "stdin": [
            "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
            "quit",
            "stats"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "no input at all",
          "stdin": "",
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Bye."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "The loop is `while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null) { ... }`, and `Bye.` goes after its closing brace.",
        "`int space = line.IndexOf(' ');` then `command` is `line.Substring(0, space)` (or the whole line when `space < 0`). A `switch (command)` picks the action.",
        "For `add`: `string[] parts = rest.Split('|');`, `books++;`, `copies += int.Parse(parts[4]);`, print `$\"Added: {parts[1]} ({int.Parse(parts[3])})\"`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Never trust input",
      "body": [
        "`int.Parse(\"nineteen\")` throws an exception and the whole program dies, which is the last thing a librarian wants in the middle of the day. Input is checked with **TryParse**, which returns `false` instead of crashing, and hands back the number through an `out` variable:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out int year) || year < 1450 || year > 2026)",
        "{",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026\");",
        "    break;   // leave this case, keep the loop running",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "`||` stops at the first `true`, so `year` is only compared once parsing has succeeded. Check the **shape** first (enough fields?), then each field. Report the first problem and carry on with the next command.",
        "",
        "Two more touches: commands should not care about case (`ADD` works like `add`), so lower-case the command with `ToLowerInvariant()`; and `stats` can track the **oldest** year seen with a variable that starts at `int.MaxValue`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Which `add` lines should be rejected?",
      "buckets": [
        "Accepted",
        "Rejected"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`add 1|Emma|Jane Austen|1815|2`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`add 1|Emma|Jane Austen|eighteen|2`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`add 1|Emma|Jane Austen|1815|0`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`add 1|Emma|Jane Austen|1815`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`add 1| |Jane Austen|1815|2`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`add 1|Emma|Jane Austen|2026|1`",
          0
        ]
      ],
      "explain": "A year that is not a number, zero copies, a missing field and a blank title are all rejected. 2026 is the current year, so it is still allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "carry": true,
      "title": "Validate everything",
      "prompt": [
        "Make `add` safe, and polish the loop.",
        "",
        "1. Commands are **case-insensitive**: `ADD`, `Stats` and `QUIT` work.",
        "2. `add` checks, in this order, and prints the first error only:",
        "   - not exactly 5 fields: `Error: use add isbn|title|author|year|copies`",
        "   - blank title: `Error: title is required`",
        "   - year not a whole number from 1450 to 2026: `Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026`",
        "   - copies not a whole number of at least 1: `Error: copies must be a whole number of at least 1`",
        "",
        "   A rejected book is not counted.",
        "3. `stats` also prints the oldest year: `Books: 2 | Copies: 5 | Oldest: 1937`. With no books it prints just `Books: 0 | Copies: 0`.",
        "",
        "Input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
        "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|nineteen|2",
        "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|0",
        "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert",
        "add 978-0441172719| |Frank Herbert|1965|2",
        "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|2",
        "stats",
        "```",
        "",
        "Output:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
        "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
        "Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026",
        "Error: copies must be a whole number of at least 1",
        "Error: use add isbn|title|author|year|copies",
        "Error: title is required",
        "Added: Dune (1965)",
        "Books: 2 | Copies: 5 | Oldest: 1937",
        "Bye.",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "string library = \"Shelfwise\";",
        "int version = 1;",
        "int books = 0;",
        "int copies = 0;",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{library} v{version}. Type help for commands.\");",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line == \"\") continue;",
        "",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string command = space < 0 ? line : line.Substring(0, space);",
        "    string rest = space < 0 ? \"\" : line.Substring(space + 1).Trim();",
        "",
        "    if (command == \"quit\") break;",
        "",
        "    switch (command)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"help\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine(\"Commands: add, stats, help, quit\");",
        "            break;",
        "        case \"add\":",
        "        {",
        "            string[] parts = rest.Split('|');",
        "            int year = int.Parse(parts[3]);",
        "            int count = int.Parse(parts[4]);",
        "            books++;",
        "            copies += count;",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Added: {parts[1]} ({year})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"stats\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Books: {books} | Copies: {copies}\");",
        "            break;",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Unknown command: {command}\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Bye.\");"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "string library = \"Shelfwise\";",
        "int version = 1;",
        "int books = 0;",
        "int copies = 0;",
        "int oldest = int.MaxValue;",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{library} v{version}. Type help for commands.\");",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line == \"\") continue;",
        "",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string command = (space < 0 ? line : line.Substring(0, space)).ToLowerInvariant();",
        "    string rest = space < 0 ? \"\" : line.Substring(space + 1).Trim();",
        "",
        "    if (command == \"quit\") break;",
        "",
        "    switch (command)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"help\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine(\"Commands: add, stats, help, quit\");",
        "            break;",
        "        case \"add\":",
        "        {",
        "            string[] parts = rest.Split('|');",
        "            if (parts.Length != 5)",
        "            {",
        "                Console.WriteLine(\"Error: use add isbn|title|author|year|copies\");",
        "                break;",
        "            }",
        "            if (parts[1].Trim() == \"\")",
        "            {",
        "                Console.WriteLine(\"Error: title is required\");",
        "                break;",
        "            }",
        "            if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out int year) || year < 1450 || year > 2026)",
        "            {",
        "                Console.WriteLine(\"Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026\");",
        "                break;",
        "            }",
        "            if (!int.TryParse(parts[4], out int count) || count < 1)",
        "            {",
        "                Console.WriteLine(\"Error: copies must be a whole number of at least 1\");",
        "                break;",
        "            }",
        "            books++;",
        "            copies += count;",
        "            if (year < oldest) oldest = year;",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Added: {parts[1]} ({year})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"stats\":",
        "            Console.WriteLine(books == 0 ? \"Books: 0 | Copies: 0\" : $\"Books: {books} | Copies: {copies} | Oldest: {oldest}\");",
        "            break;",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"Unknown command: {command}\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Bye.\");"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "every kind of bad add",
          "stdin": [
            "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3",
            "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|nineteen|2",
            "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|0",
            "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert",
            "add 978-0441172719| |Frank Herbert|1965|2",
            "add 978-0441172719|Dune|Frank Herbert|1965|2",
            "stats"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
            "Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026",
            "Error: copies must be a whole number of at least 1",
            "Error: use add isbn|title|author|year|copies",
            "Error: title is required",
            "Added: Dune (1965)",
            "Books: 2 | Copies: 5 | Oldest: 1937",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "commands in any case",
          "stdin": [
            "STATS",
            "Add 978-0141439518|Emma|Jane Austen|1815|1",
            "HELP",
            "Stats",
            "QUIT",
            "stats"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Books: 0 | Copies: 0",
            "Added: Emma (1815)",
            "Commands: add, stats, help, quit",
            "Books: 1 | Copies: 1 | Oldest: 1815",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "years outside the range",
          "stdin": [
            "add 1|Old|Someone|1449|1",
            "add 2|Future|Someone|2027|1",
            "add 3|Gutenberg Bible|Unknown|1450|1",
            "stats"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026",
            "Error: year must be a number from 1450 to 2026",
            "Added: Gutenberg Bible (1450)",
            "Books: 1 | Copies: 1 | Oldest: 1450",
            "Bye."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "the earlier behaviour still works",
          "stdin": [
            "help",
            "dance",
            "add 978-0261103344|The Hobbit|J.R.R. Tolkien|1937|3"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Shelfwise v1. Type help for commands.",
            "Commands: add, stats, help, quit",
            "Unknown command: dance",
            "Added: The Hobbit (1937)",
            "Bye."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Each check is an `if` that prints its error and then `break;`s out of the `case`, so later checks and the counting do not run.",
        "`if (!int.TryParse(parts[3], out int year) || year < 1450 || year > 2026) { ... }` works because `||` stops as soon as one side is true.",
        "Lower-case the command where you cut it out of the line: `(...).ToLowerInvariant()`. For stats: `books == 0 ? \"Books: 0 | Copies: 0\" : $\"... | Oldest: {oldest}\"`."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
